# Everything not listed here is sent to Docker as build context on every build. Keep out what the
# Dockerfile never COPYs -- the ultimate/ source tree alone is ~6 GB -- and all build products.

# Version control and the Ultimate sources (the image uses the prebuilt releases in tools/)
.git
**/.git
ultimate

# Local results and experiment data (pre-computed results ship in logs/)
stats
output
test-reports
# Lasso traces Ultimate dumped into a release directory, its working directory. Anchored on tools/:
# benchmarks/smoke_test/ ships pre-extracted lassos under similar names on purpose.
tools/*/lasso_traces
# Eclipse caches that Ultimate writes into a release's configuration/ when it runs on the host. The
# release itself ships only config.ini and org.eclipse.update there.
tools/UAutomizer-PaSTTeL-linux/configuration/org.eclipse.core.runtime
tools/UAutomizer-PaSTTeL-linux/configuration/org.eclipse.equinox.app
tools/UAutomizer-PaSTTeL-linux/configuration/org.eclipse.osgi

# Build products: the image compiles PaSTTeL from source, against the solvers it installs itself.
# A host-built pasttel/bin/pasttel links the host's libraries, and COPY keeps file timestamps, so a
# leftover *.o could make `make` skip the rebuild entirely.
pasttel/bin
**/*.o
**/*.d
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.smt2

# Solvers are installed from their release archives; the extracted copies next to them are unused.
tools/solvers/*
!tools/solvers/*.zip
